.72 | 0.55 | 0.055 | 0.126 | 0.127 | 0.298 |","+| cover `(6, 1)` | `β* + 0.1` | 24 | 15 | 9, 5, 4 | 8% | 20 | 154.2 | 1538 | 21.84 | 63.45 ± 11.47 | 62.97 | 0.61 | 0.125 | 0.173 | 0.173 | 0.322 |","+| cover `(6, 1)` | `β* + 0.1` | 28 | 17 | 11, 6, 5 | 4% | 28.5 | 206.9 | 3498 | 28.42 | 110.01 ± 22.61 | 124.86 | 0.65 | 0.120 | 0.168 | 0.172 | 0.304 |","+","+What the table says:","+","+- **The formula and the enumerator agree.** In every uncensored cell the","+  sample mean of `X′` is within two standard errors of `E[X²]/E[X] − 1`","+  (26 of 26; the two cells with censored rows are below the prediction by","+  the censoring, as they must be). The second moment of §8.5 is therefore","+  the planted mean, measured, and the enumerator counts what the formula","+  counts.","+- **The mean is carried by the tail.** The top 10% of instances carry","+  64–94% of `ΣX′` in every cell; at `G(32, 6/32)`, `β*`, the median is 64","+  against a mean of 1,479 and a maximum of 120,314. The planted mean is","+  not what a planted instance looks like.","+- **At `β*` the median planted instance has a small cluster.** `G(n, 6/n)`:","+  median `X′` = 2, 3, 19, 39, 64 at `n = 16 … 32`; `G(n, 10/n)`: 0, 0, 1, 1,","+  5.5 (the \"1\" is the reversed pair where `N` is even); covers `(6, 1)`:","+  **`X′ = 1` at every size, the reversed pair and nothing else** (`N` is","+  even in all four cells), with `X′ ≥ 2` on 42–47% of instances and `X′ = 1`","+  on the rest. At `β* + 0.1` the counts are large everywhere (median","+  11,067 at `G(32, 6/32)`), but there `E[X] = e^{g n}` with `g > 0` and the","+  other pairs are the instance's own population, not a cluster of `P₀`","+  (§4.4).","+- **Finite sizes.** The exact planted mean's exponent at `n = 32` is","+  `0.23` (`c = 6`), `0.15` (`c = 10`), `0.11` (covers, `n = 28`) against","+  asymptotic `0.35, 0.31, 0.22`: at these `n` nothing is near its limit,","+  and the asymptotic `0.23` of §8.5 (a) is at `n = ∞`; the finite exact","+  value is what the medians are compared with.","+","+### 4.3 Growth in `n`, and the fork","+","+OLS slopes in `n` (nats per vertex, fitted over five sizes for the cell","+statistics and over 645–987 instances for the per-instance one; `slopes.csv`):","+","+| model | `β` | sizes | slope `log(median X′)` | slope `log E[X′]` | slope `log(mean X′)` | per-instance slope `log X′` (`X′ > 0`) | at the largest `n`: `log med / n` | `log E / n` | ratio |","+|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|","+| cover `(6, 1)` | `β*` | 16–28 | 0.000 ± 0.000 | 0.163 ± 0.003 | 0.192 ± 0.009 | 0.094 ± 0.010 | 0.000 | 0.109 | **0.00** |","+| cover `(6, 1)` | `β* + 0.1` | 16–28 | 0.299 ± 0.051 | 0.265 ± 0.032 | 0.263 ± 0.035 | 0.216 ± 0.012 | 0.120 | 0.172 | **0.69** |","+| `G(n, 6/n)` | `β*` | 16–32 | 0.237 ± 0.033 | 0.313 ± 0.034 | 0.307 ± 0.015 | 0.172 ± 0.012 | 0.130 | 0.229 | **0.57** |","+| `G(n, 6/n)` | `β* + 0.1` | 16–32 | 0.450 ± 0.050 | 0.542 ± 0.031 | 0.475 ± 0.039 | 0.450 ± 0.012 | 0.291 | 0.386 | **0.75** |","+| `G(n, 10/n)` | `β*` | 16–32 | 0.213 ± 0.123 | 0.296 ± 0.027 | 0.276 ± 0.045 | 0.116 ± 0.013 | 0.053 | 0.147 | **0.36** |","+| `G(n, 10/n)` | `β* + 0.1` | 16–32 | 0.321 ± 0.029 | 0.396 ± 0.026 | 0.375 ± 0.010 | 0.249 ± 0.012 | 0.170 | 0.245 | **0.69** |","+","+**The fork, by the item's letter** (`log(median X′)/n` against `log","+E[X′ | planted]/n` at the largest `n`): ratio **0.57** at `G(32, 6/32)`,","+`β*` (within a factor 2 — \"typical\"); **0.36** at `G(32, 10/32)`, `β*`","+(between a quarter and a half — \"both\"); **0 on covers at `β*`** (the","+median has no pair beyond the reverse at any size — \"artefact\"); 0.69–0.75","+at `β* + 0.1` (\"typical\", but see §4.4: there the pairs are not a cluster","+of `P₀`). The growth rates say the same with less noise: at `β*` the","+median grows at `0.24 ± 0.03` (`c = 6`) against the mean's `0.31 ± 0.03`,","+and the per-instance geometric mean at `0.17 ± 0.01` (`c = 6`) and `0.12 ±","+0.01` (`c = 10`) against `0.31` and `0.28`; on covers the median does not","+grow at all (`0.00`) against `0.16`. So at `β*`: **the cluster exists on","+the typical planted instance and grows exponentially on `G(n, c/n)` at","+roughly half the mean's rate, and does not grow at all on the `(6, 1)`","+covers, where §8.5's `e^{0.23 n}` lives.** The second moment at `(6, 1)`","+is a rare-instance artefact; on `G(n, c/n)` it is half typical and half","+tail, and the \"in between\" branch of the fork applies.","+","+### 4.4 Where the other pairs are: two lobes, and an empty middle","+","+![Hamming distance of the other exact-size empty pairs from the planted pair, per cell at the largest n](scratch/separator_moment/04_planted/distance_hist.png)","+","+*Distance from the planted pair in units of `n`, pooled over the 200","+planted instances of each cell at the largest `n` (`distance_hist.csv`);","+the solid line is the far/near cut at `0.2 n`, the dashed line the","+position of the reversed pair, `N/n`.*","+","+At `β*` the histogram is **bimodal with an empty middle**: one lobe at","+`d ≈ 0.1–0.4 n` (perturbations of `P₀`), one at `d ≈ N/n ± 0.15` (perturbations","+of the reversed pair), and almost nothing at `d ≈ 0.5–0.6 n` on `G(32, 6/32)`","+(3,000 of 295,701 pairs at `d = 17–19`) and nothing at all on covers","+(`d = 10–11`: one pair of 4,584). At `β* + 0.1` on `G(n, c/n)` the middle","+fills and the distribution is broad and unimodal around `0.55–0.6 n`:","+the other pairs are then the instance's whole pair population. The shares","+(pooled over pairs; `cells.csv`):","+","+| model | `β` | `n` | share far (`d > 0.2 n`) | within `0.05 n` of `P₀` / of `P₀` or its reverse | `0.1 n` | `0.2 n` | `0.3 n` | per-instance median share within `0.2 n` of `P₀` or reverse | far pairs with `∣A′ ∩ R∣ ≥ ∣A′ ∩ A∣` | median move-class of `P₀` (max) | `X/X₄` |","+|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|","+| `G(n, 6/n)` | `β*` | 16 | 0.77 | 0.000 / 0.000 | 0.000 / 0.033 | 0.234 / 0.434 | 0.390 / 0.675 | 0.79 | 0.53 | 1 (356) | 1.81 |","+| `G(n, 6/n)` | `β*` | 24 | 0.87 | 0.000 / 0.008 | 0.039 / 0.086 | 0.134 / 0.276 | 0.295 / 0.598 | 0.86 | 0.59 | 2 (1423) | 3.50 |","+| `G(n, 6/n)` | `β*` | 28 | 0.90 | 0.000 / 0.001 | 0.012 / 0.020 | 0.102 / 0.183 | 0.296 / 0.548 | 0.63 | 0.54 | 9 (10680) | 4.79 |","+| `G(n, 6/n)` | `β*` | 32 | 0.90 | 0.000 / 0.001 | 0.011 / 0.019 | 0.098 / 0.176 | 0.289 / 0.507 | 0.88 | 0.50 | 8 (71548) | 5.17 |","+| `G(n, 6/n)` | `β* + 0.1` | 16 | 0.93 | 0.000 / 0.015 | 0.000 / 0.015 | 0.073 / 0.162 | 0.137 / 0.290 | 0.55 | 0.60 | 1 (3810) | 2.76 |","+| `G(n, 6/n)` | `β* + 0.1` | 24 | 0.97 | 0.000 / 0.001 | 0.006 / 0.013 | 0.034 / 0.068 | 0.160 / 0.322 | 0.24 | 0.54 | 37.5 (25712) | 7.38 |","+| `G(n, 6/n)` | `β* + 0.1` | 28 | 0.99 | 0.000 / 0.000 | 0.001 / 0.002 | 0.012 / 0.024 | 0.082 / 0.163 | 0.07 | 0.54 | 1151 (243332) | 16.44 |","+| `G(n, 6/n)` | `β* + 0.1` | 32 | 0.99 | 0.000 / 0.000 | 0.001 / 0.001 | 0.012 / 0.023 | 0.062 / 0.122 | 0.08 | 0.51 | 4196 (267543) | 20.38 |","+| `G(n, 10/n)` | `β*` | 16 | 0.43 | 0.000 / 0.000 | 0.000 / 0.066 | 0.572 / 0.958 | 0.602 / 1.000 | 1.00 | 0.93 | 1 (7) | 1.15 |","+| `G(n, 10/n)` | `β*` | 24 | 0.68 | 0.000 / 0.086 | 0.160 / 0.406 | 0.320 / 0.726 | 0.421 / 0.929 | 1.00 | 0.80 | 1 (125) | 1.66 |","+| `G(n, 10/n)` | `β*` | 28 | 0.84 | 0.000 / 0.004 | 0.046 / 0.074 | 0.156 / 0.289 | 0.357 / 0.711 | 1.00 | 0.60 | 1 (2759) | 1.87 |","+| `G(n, 10/n)` | `β*` | 32 | 0.64 | 0.000 / 0.004 | 0.102 / 0.175 | 0.361 / 0.672 | 0.493 / 0.903 | 1.00 | 0.72 | 1 (654) | 2.19 |","+| `G(n, 10/n)` | `β* + 0.1` | 16 | 0.73 | 0.000 / 0.000 | 0.000 / 0.028 | 0.267 / 0.481 | 0.445 / 0.766 | 1.00 | 0.55 | 1 (96) | 1.36 |","+| `G(n, 10/n)` | `β* + 0.1` | 24 | 0.89 | 0.000 / 0.013 | 0.039 / 0.091 | 0.112 / 0.237 | 0.262 / 0.537 | 0.78 | 0.57 | 1 (1407) | 2.37 |","+| `G(n, 10/n)` | `β* + 0.1` | 28 | 0.90 | 0.000 / 0.003 | 0.016 / 0.034 | 0.095 / 0.193 | 0.278 / 0.558 | 0.46 | 0.57 | 9 (5652) | 3.54 |","+| `G(n, 10/n)` | `β* + 0.1` | 32 | 0.94 | 0.000 / 0.001 | 0.006 / 0.013 | 0.059 / 0.119 | 0.159 / 0.319 | 0.34 | 0.55 | 19 (67758) | 4.05 |","+| cover `(6, 1)` | `β*` | 16 | 0.74 | 0.000 / 0.418 | 0.000 / 0.418 | 0.264 / 0.946 | 0.291 / 1.000 | 1.00 | 0.96 | 1 (15) | 1.28 |","+| cover `(6, 1)` | `β*` | 28 | 0.63 | 0.000 / 0.044 | 0.158 / 0.359 | 0.370 / 0.784 | 0.478 / 1.000 | 1.00 | 0.83 | 1 (456) | 2.92 |","+| cover `(6, 1)` | `β* + 0.1` | 16 | 0.71 | 0.000 / 0.176 | 0.000 / 0.176 | 0.292 / 0.759 | 0.390 / 0.951 | 1.00 | 0.84 | 1 (20) | 1.98 |","+| cover `(6, 1)` | `β* + 0.1` | 28 | 0.77 | 0.000 / 0.002 | 0.060 / 0.082 | 0.227 / 0.328 | 0.567 / 0.810 | 0.70 | 0.42 | 7.5 (2898) | 5.90 |","+","+Three readings. (i) **Few other pairs are small perturbations of `P₀`","+alone**: within `0.1 n` of `P₀` itself sit 2–9% of the other pairs on","+`G(n, c/n)` at `β*`; within `0.1 n` of `P₀` *or its reverse*, 2–18% on the","+graphs and 36–73% on covers. Within `0.3 n` of either, 51% (`c = 6`), 90%","+(`c = 10`) and 99.96% (covers) at the largest `n`. (ii) **The per-instance","+median is tighter than the pool**: on the median planted instance at","+`β*`, 88% (`c = 6`), 100% (`c = 10`, covers) of the other pairs sit within","+`0.2 n` of `P₀` or its reverse, against 18%, 67%, 78% pooled — the far pairs","+belong to the rare instances with large `X′`, which is the tail of §4.2","+again. (iii) **The reversed pair is half the cluster.** At `c = 6` the far","+pairs split evenly between the two orientations (50–54% have `|A′ ∩ R| ≥","+|A′ ∩ A|`); at `c = 10` and on covers the reversed lobe dominates (72%,","+83%). The move-class of `P₀` (single swaps) holds 8–9 pairs at the median","+on `G(n, 6/n)`, `β*` (max 71,548), and 1 — `P₀` alone — at `c = 10` and on","+covers; `X/X₄` is 1.2–5.2 at `β*` and up to 20 at `β* + 0.1`.","+","+The far and near pairs have different mean overlap tables","+(`overlap_far_near.csv`, `n = 32`, `c = 6`, `β*`, in units of `n`): near","+pairs keep `A ∩ A′ = 0.39`, `R ∩ R′ = 0.36`, `S ∩ S′ = 0.095` with","+`A ∩ R′ = R ∩ A′ = 0.02` (`P₀` with a few swaps); far pairs average `A ∩ A′","+= A ∩ R′ = R ∩ A′ = 0.19` — the average of the two lobes, not a table any","+pair has. At `c = 10` the far table is the reversed pair's (`A ∩ R′ = R ∩","+A′ = 0.21`, `A ∩ A′ = 0.08`), which is §8.5 (a)'s extremal table with","+`S ∩ S′ = 0.25` of `|S| = 0.34 n`.","+","+### 4.5 The mechanism","+","+For every far pair, the vertices of `S` that joined a side (`S ∩ (A′ ∪","+R′)`), their degree into the planted sides `A ∪ R`, and how many of those","+neighbours were *evicted* into `S′` (a side neighbour of a vertex now in","+`A′` must be in `A′` or in `S′`); against the degree law of all `S`","+vertices (`mechanism.csv`, `mechanism_summary.csv`; the mechanism is","+sampled at 200,000 far pairs per instance where there are more):","+","+| model | `β` | `n` | moved `S` vertices (far pairs) | their planted-side degree: mean | share `≤ 1` | all `S` vertices: mean | share `≤ 1` | evicted neighbours: mean | share 0 | share `≤ 1` |","+|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|","+| `G(n, 6/n)` | `β*` | 16 | 3,141 | 2.87 | 0.23 | 4.95 | 0.017 | 0.80 | 0.42 | 0.80 |","+| `G(n, 6/n)` | `β*` | 32 | 864,223 | 2.67 | 0.24 | 5.11 | 0.028 | 0.64 | 0.51 | 0.87 |","+| `G(n, 6/n)` | `β* + 0.1` | 16 | 24,378 | 2.21 | 0.35 | 4.53 | 0.028 | 0.83 | 0.38 | 0.82 |","+| `G(n, 6/n)` | `β* + 0.1` | 32 | 38,802,029 | 3.07 | 0.14 | 4.29 | 0.056 | 1.11 | 0.30 | 0.69 |","+| `G(n, 10/n)` | `β*` | 16 | 65 | 3.79 | 0.00 | 6.83 | 0.000 | 0.69 | 0.42 | 0.89 |","+| `G(n, 10/n)` | `β*` | 32 | 17,567 | 4.45 | 0.02 | 6.59 | 0.004 | 1.35 | 0.18 | 0.60 |","+| `G(n, 10/n)` | `β* + 0.1` | 16 | 1,136 | 3.18 | 0.09 | 5.58 | 0.003 | 1.29 | 0.17 | 0.64 |","+| `G(n, 10/n)` | `β* + 0.1` | 32 | 1,697,525 | 3.80 | 0.03 | 5.68 | 0.009 | 1.91 | 0.10 | 0.38 |","+| cover `(6, 1)` | `β*` | 28 | 5,636 | 5.10 | 0.00 | 9.09 | 0.000 | 1.27 | 0.21 | 0.64 |","+| cover `(6, 1)` | `β* + 0.1` | 28 | 58,721 | 4.25 | 0.04 | 6.72 | 0.004 | 2.08 | 0.07 | 0.33 |","+","+**The hypothesis holds in direction and not in its strong form.** The","+separator vertices that recombine into a side have about half the","+planted-side degree of a typical `S` vertex (2.7 against 5.1 at `c = 6`,","+4.4 against 6.6 at `c = 10`, 5.1 against 9.1 on covers at `β*`), but they","+are not degree-zero vertices: only 1–2% have no side neighbour, 2–24%","+have at most one. What is small is the number they *evict*: at `β*` the","+moved vertex evicts no neighbour in 18–51% of cases and at most one in","+60–87%, with a mean of 0.6–1.4 — the rest of its side neighbours are on","+its own new side. So the recombination is \"a low-degree separator vertex","+whose side neighbours mostly lie on one side joins that side, pushing","+one or two of its other-side neighbours into the separator\", and on the","+reversed lobe the same with the sides exchanged.","+","+### 4.6 The union bound's slack, measured directly","+","+By identity 2, `P(X > 0)/E[X] = E[1/X | P₀ empty]`, and the planted sample","+gives it with a standard error of `0.01–0.03` (`cells.csv`,","+`inv_X_mean`). The conversion to `β` uses the pair exponent's slope at","+`β*`: `3.38` per unit of `β` at `c = 6`, `3.30` at `c = 10`, `2.82` on","+`(6, 1)` covers (computed here by central differences of","+`gnp_pair_rate` / `rate`; the header's `3.3–3.4` for `c = 6–10`).","+","+| model | `β` | `n` | `E_planted[1/X]` ± se | `−log E_planted[1/X]` (nats) | per vertex | in `β` | `log E[X′ ∣ planted] / n` |","+|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|","+| `G(n, 6/n)` | `β*` | 16 | 0.453 ± 0.027 | 0.79 | 0.050 | 0.015 | 0.175 |","+| `G(n, 6/n)` | `β*` | 20 | 0.337 ± 0.025 | 1.09 | 0.054 | 0.016 | 0.170 |","+| `G(n, 6/n)` | `β*` | 24 | 0.155 ± 0.013 | 1.86 | 0.078 | 0.023 | 0.213 |","+| `G(n, 6/n)` | `β*` | 28 | 0.116 ± 0.016 | 2.15 | 0.077 | 0.023 | 0.244 |","+| `G(n, 6/n)` | `β*` | 32 | 0.124 ± 0.018 | 2.08 | 0.065 | 0.019 | 0.229 |","+| `G(n, 6/n)` | `β* + 0.1` | 16 | 0.183 ± 0.014 | 1.70 | 0.106 | 0.031 | 0.245 |","+| `G(n, 6/n)` | `β* + 0.1` | 20 | 0.105 ± 0.014 | 2.25 | 0.113 | 0.033 | 0.284 |","+| `G(n, 6/n)` | `β* + 0.1` | 24 | 0.043 ± 0.007 | 3.14 | 0.131 | 0.039 | 0.312 |","+| `G(n, 6/n)` | `β* + 0.1` | 28 | 0.004 ± 0.001 | 5.41 | 0.193 | 0.057 | 0.375 |","+| `G(n, 6/n)` | `β* + 0.1` | 32 | 0.003 ± 0.001 | 5.95 | 0.186 | 0.055 | 0.386 |","+| `G(n, 10/n)` | `β*` | 16 | 0.835 ± 0.021 | 0.18 | 0.011 | 0.003 | -0.022 |","+| `G(n, 10/n)` | `β*` | 20 | 0.667 ± 0.027 | 0.41 | 0.020 | 0.006 | 0.072 |","+| `G(n, 10/n)` | `β*` | 24 | 0.344 ± 0.014 | 1.07 | 0.044 | 0.013 | 0.102 |","+| `G(n, 10/n)` | `β*` | 28 | 0.499 ± 0.029 | 0.70 | 0.025 | 0.008 | 0.111 |","+| `G(n, 10/n)` | `β*` | 32 | 0.291 ± 0.024 | 1.23 | 0.039 | 0.012 | 0.147 |","+| `G(n, 10/n)` | `β* + 0.1` | 16 | 0.613 ± 0.027 | 0.49 | 0.031 | 0.009 | 0.079 |","+| `G(n, 10/n)` | `β* + 0.1` | 20 | 0.260 ± 0.023 | 1.35 | 0.067 | 0.020 | 0.162 |","+| `G(n, 10/n)` | `β* + 0.1` | 24 | 0.176 ± 0.014 | 1.74 | 0.072 | 0.022 | 0.171 |","+| `G(n, 10/n)` | `β* + 0.1` | 28 | 0.081 ± 0.010 | 2.51 | 0.090 | 0.027 | 0.212 |","+| `G(n, 10/n)` | `β* + 0.1` | 32 | 0.039 ± 0.007 | 3.25 | 0.102 | 0.031 | 0.245 |","+| cover `(6, 1)` | `β*` | 16 | 0.439 ± 0.010 | 0.82 | 0.051 | 0.018 | 0.069 |","+| cover `(6, 1)` | `β*` | 20 | 0.416 ± 0.012 | 0.88 | 0.044 | 0.016 | 0.086 |","+| cover `(6, 1)` | `β*` | 24 | 0.348 ± 0.015 | 1.06 | 0.044 | 0.016 | 0.099 |","+| cover `(6, 1)` | `β*` | 28 | 0.298 ± 0.016 | 1.21 | 0.043 | 0.015 | 0.109 |","+| cover `(6, 1)` | `β* + 0.1` | 16 | 0.323 ± 0.014 | 1.13 | 0.071 | 0.025 | 0.115 |","+| cover `(6, 1)` | `β* + 0.1` | 20 | 0.274 ± 0.015 | 1.29 | 0.065 | 0.023 | 0.127 |","+| cover `(6, 1)` | `β* + 0.1` | 24 | 0.172 ± 0.020 | 1.76 | 0.073 | 0.026 | 0.173 |","+| cover `(6, 1)` | `β* + 0.1` | 28 | 0.117 ± 0.015 | 2.15 | 0.077 | 0.027 | 0.172 |","+","+At `β*` and the largest sizes the union bound is loose by **0.065 nats","+per vertex at `c = 6`, 0.039 at `c = 10`, 0.043 on `(6, 1)` covers** —","+**0.019, 0.012 and 0.015 in `β`** — against planted-mean exponents of","+0.23, 0.15 and 0.11 that the second-moment ratio would suggest. The","+total slack in nats (`−log E[1/X]`) is 0.8, 1.1, 1.9, 2.2, 2.1 at `n = 16","+… 32` on `G(n, 6/n)` and 0.8, 0.9, 1.1, 1.2 on covers at `n = 16 … 28`:","+growing slowly and sub-linearly at these sizes, so the per-vertex figures","+above are upper estimates of the rate and the limit is not determined by","+this instrument. The rows at `β* + 0.1` are not a gain in the constant:","+there `E[X] = e^{g n}` with `g > 0` and `E[X]/P(X > 0) ≥ E[X]`.","+","+This is the number items 09, 11 and 12 need, and it is small: the *entire*","+union-bound slack at these cells, if the per-vertex figure held","+asymptotically, is `0.012–0.019` in `β`, below the brief's kill of `0.02`","+for any single representative count and consistent with §3's prediction","+(`≤ 0.003` for the separator and closure) plus the reversed lobe (a factor","+2 where `N` is even) plus the component flips. The ideal weighted count","+`Y = Σ_P 1[P empty]/X` is exactly `1[X > 0]`, so no choice of `Z ≤ X` in","+item 09 can gain more than this at the same `(n, k)`.","+","+### 4.7 Kill verdict (the fork), and what it sends on","+","+**Stated as a fork, decided per model.** On `G(n, c/n)` at `β*` the","+ratio is 0.57 (`c = 6`) and 0.36 (`c = 10`): the letter says \"typical\" at","+`c = 6` and \"in between\" at `c = 10`; the growth rates (median at about","+half the mean's rate; per-instance geometric mean at 0.4–0.55 of it) put","+both in the item's middle branch, and **both are written up with the","+numbers**. On `(6, 1)` covers at `β*` the median `X′` is 1 — the reversed","+pair — at every size and the ratio is 0: **the `e^{0.23 n}` of §8.5 (a)","+is a rare-instance artefact of `E[X²]` on the cell it was computed for**,","+and the closed-pair count is near-tight for `P(X > 0)` there in the sense","+of identity 2: the union bound's measured slack is `0.04` nats per vertex","+(`0.015` in `β`).","+","+For **item 09**: the weighted count's gain is bounded by §4.6 at these","+sizes (`0.012–0.019` in `β` at `β*`), and the planted lower tail is","+dominated by instances with `X ≤ 2` (the pair and its reverse) on covers","+(53–58% of planted instances) and by `X ≤ 65` on `G(32, 6/32)`: item 09 is","+reduced to the paragraph the fork prescribes, with the Laplace-transform","+computation optional. For **item 12**: say that `P(X > 0)` is within","+`e^{0.04–0.07 n}` of `E[X]` at `n ≤ 32` (measured, by identity 2), that the","+remaining gap to the fitted slopes (`0.08–0.10` in `β` on `G(n, c/n)`,","+`0.06` on `(6, 1)`) is therefore mostly the **necessary condition** — empty","+pairs exist on instances whose pathwidth is larger — and not the union","+bound; and that the cluster around a planted pair is two lobes (the pair","+and its reverse, each with its single-swap perturbations) with an empty","+middle at `β*`.","+","+### 4.8 Regenerate, size range, what this does not claim","+","+* **Regenerate.** `nice -n 19 python3 reports/scratch/separator_moment/04_planted/run.py --workers 8`","+  (stages `run`, `stats`, `draw`; 305 + 1 + 1 s; `--probe` times the","+  largest cells on three instances each); `python3 -m pytest","+  tests/test_separator_moment.py` (50 tests, 14 new: planting deletes","+  exactly the forbidden edges and is symmetric and idempotent; the planted","+  cover meets at most one side per pattern; the overlap table sums to `n`,","+  agrees with `overlap_tables` and with the Hamming distance; `lq_sides`","+  against `lq` and against counting; `second_moment_exact_cover` against","+  `second_moment_exact` at `r = t − 1`; identity 1 against simulation and","+  against the finite forms; identity 2 on every labelled graph at `n = 6`;","+  `beta_star_gnp` against the record).","+* **Size range.** `n = 16–32` planted `G(n, c/n)` at `c = 6, 10`; `n =","+  16–28` planted `(6, 1)` covers; `β ∈ {β*, β* + 0.1}` rounded to integer","+  `k`; 200 instances per cell.","+* **Does not claim.** A value of `P(X > 0)` or `P(pw ≤ k)`: the planted","+  law weights instances by `X`. Anything asymptotic: the fork is decided","+  at `n ≤ 32` with the growth in `n` beside it, the per-vertex slack of","+  §4.6 is sub-linear in `n` over the range and is an upper estimate of its","+  rate, and the exact planted mean at `n = 32` is itself a third below its","+  limit. That the mechanism of §4.5 is the only one: it is the dominant","+  one on far pairs at these sizes. That `β_sep` or `β_closed` fail item","+  06's kill — §4.6 makes that likelier than §3 did, and item 06 decides","+  it. That the `0.23` of §8.5 (a) is wrong: it is the planted mean's","+  asymptotic exponent and this item measured its finite form exactly","+  (identity 1) and found it correct; what is withdrawn is the reading that","+  it is the typical cluster."]}]},{"filePath":"/home/al/dev/MOSP/reports/scratch/separator_moment/04_planted/tables.md","hunks":[{"oldStart":1,"oldLines":107,"newStart":1,"newLines":0,"lines":["-TABLE1","-| model | `β` | `n` | `k` | `N`, `t`, `r` | `X′ = 0` | median `X′` | p90 | max | gm (`X′ > 0`) | mean ± se | `E[X′ ∣ planted]` | top 10% share of `ΣX′` | `log med / n` | `log mean / n` | `log E / n` | asymptotic `sup − g` |","-|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|","-| `G(n, 6/n)` | `β*` | 16 | 3 | 13, 7, 6 | 30% | 2 | 29.1 | 486 | 5.72 | 12.37 ± 2.79 | 16.49 | 0.64 | 0.043 | 0.157 | 0.175 | 0.396 |","-| `G(n, 6/n)` | `β*` | 20 | 3 | 17, 9, 8 | 18% | 3 | 62.1 | 1493 | 8.99 | 42.32 ± 10.84 | 29.7 | 0.79 | 0.055 | 0.187 | 0.170 | 0.338 |","-| `G(n, 6/n)` | `β*` | 24 | 4 | 20, 10, 10 | 0% | 19 | 316.2 | 3173 | 15.96 | 126.69 ± 24.48 | 168 | 0.75 | 0.123 | 0.202 | 0.213 | 0.364 |","-| `G(n, 6/n)` | `β*` | 28 | 5 | 23, 12, 11 | 4% | 39 | 988.9 | 17712 | 54.93 | 639.75 ± 152.57 | 928.54 | 0.84 | 0.131 | 0.231 | 0.244 | 0.382 |","-| `G(n, 6/n)` | `β*` | 32 | 5 | 27, 14, 13 | 7% | 64 | 737.4 | 120314 | 70.02 | 1478.51 ± 655.35 | 1538 | 