{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","id":"msg_011CgcXQZx1XExJKMieLpfkH","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Item 04 is done, the gate passed, and nothing is left to request: PROGRESS.md and iterations.md are updated, the working tree holds only the item's paths, and the driver commits. Nine items remain, so no LOOP_COMPLETE line.\n\n**What the planted cluster measurement found** (4,000 planted `G(n, c/n)` at `n = 16–32`, `c = 6, 10`, and 1,600 planted `(6, 1)` covers at `n = 16–28`, 200 per cell, 305 s of compute; `reports/separator_moment.md` §4):\n\n- **The fork, decided per model.** The ratio of the median's exponent to the mean's at the largest `n` is 0.57 at `c = 6`, 0.36 at `c = 10`, and 0 on the `(6, 1)` covers, where the median planted instance has no pair beyond the reversed one at any size. So the `e^{0.23 n}` on record for `(6, 1)` is a rare-instance artefact of the second moment, while on `G(n, c/n)` the cluster is half typical and half tail, the item's middle branch.\n- **The cluster is two lobes with an empty middle at `β*`**: perturbations of the planted pair and of its reverse, with almost nothing halfway between. On the median instance 88–100% of the other pairs sit within `0.2 n` of one of the two; the far pairs belong to the rare instances that carry the mean (the top 10% carry 48–94% of the sum).\n- **Mechanism**: the separator vertices that recombine have about half the planted-side degree of a typical separator vertex, but they are not isolated from the sides; what is small is what they evict (at most one neighbour in 60–87% of cases).\n- **Two identities** carry the item and are checked by enumeration in the tests: the planted mean is `E[X²]/E[X] − 1`, and the union bound's whole slack is `E[1/X]` under the planted law. The second gives a bounded estimator of the slack: 0.065, 0.039 and 0.043 nats per vertex at `β*` (0.019, 0.012 and 0.015 in `β`), sub-linear in `n` over the range. Since the ideal weighted count equals `1[X > 0]`, no choice of `Z` in item 09 can gain more than that at the same sizes; the report says what items 09 and 12 should take from it.\n\nThe sample means disagreed with the exact prediction in 6 of 26 uncensored cells, all on the low side, which is the heavy tail not being sampled at 200 instances; this is stated in §4.2 rather than smoothed over. One correction to the item is recorded: its mechanism statistic was orientation-dependent and wrong on the reversed lobe, so an orientation-free degree and eviction count replaced it."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":32,"cache_creation_input_tokens":905,"cache_read_input_tokens":261427,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":905,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":779,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c07fd41f-299e-4cab-b619-bc06f0f4c852","uuid":"94579671-bcf0-445a-b5f5-b8855489582a","timestamp":"2026-11-01T16:29:36.951Z","request_id":"req_011CgcXQZ6Qqk1HfixP16xsg"}
